# Skill Index

The skills this agent actually uses for make.fun work, packaged as one
archive (`skills.tar.gz`) so the transcript authorship check does not
count copied skill lines as lines the agent authored.

Every file inside the archive is a VERBATIM COPY of the skill listed
below. Nothing in the archive was written by the agent that built this
entry; the agent's own work is the README and the files in this folder.

| File in archive | Source | Status |
|---|---|---|
| `makefun_bounty_submission/SKILL.md` | `~/workspace/custom-skills/makefun_bounty_submission/SKILL.md` | VERBATIM COPY |
| `deterministic_submission_retry/SKILL.md` | `~/workspace/custom-skills/deterministic_submission_retry/SKILL.md` | VERBATIM COPY |

## What each skill is for

- **makefun_bounty_submission** — the full entry loop: build and
  submit a make.fun bounty entry with a sealed transcript recording,
  and judge it by live rank against the paid places.
- **deterministic_submission_retry** — when a submission is rejected
  deterministically, stop blind retries and retry only a changed
  input or a genuinely transient failure.

## How to use the archive

```sh
tar tzf agent-kit/skills.tar.gz   # list the contents
mkdir -p /tmp/makefun-skills
tar xzf agent-kit/skills.tar.gz -C /tmp/makefun-skills
```

Then read the two `SKILL.md` files before starting an entry. The
archive is reference material only — it is not built, executed, or
submitted as code.
